Aerie-Purpose: List at most the system's default speech voice from speechSynthesis.getVoices() while fingerprinting protection is on, so the voices installed on the computer are no fingerprint surface (issue #120).
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis.cc (OnSetVoiceList), third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/BUILD.gn
Aerie-Kind: hook

Uses the kNavigator token that hardening/0021 adds, so "token present" means "protected here" and the
global and per-site switches give the real voice list back with no renderer change.

SpeechSynthesis::OnSetVoiceList receives the voice list from the browser. A protected window keeps one
voice: the first one the system marks as default, or the first one when none is marked, chosen by
aerie_navigator_pins::VoiceIndexToKeep (unit tested). An empty list stays empty. The page can still
speak with the system's default voice, because speak() without an utterance voice never needed the
list, and the one voice it can list is the one the system would pick. The list is filtered when it
arrives, so voiceschanged fires with the short list too.

The size of the real list depends on the speech engine. On Linux Chrome gets its voices from
speech-dispatcher, so a computer with no speech engine installed lists none, and the Bench
(hardening_fingerprinting_navigator) says "not distinguishable" for voices when the system lists one
or none.

